313316-9597-51ca-aef9-180a07153133" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "unbounded above" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489548} {:answer/id #uuid "b49aa992-7767-5ec1-abc9-7e510c2fae46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "bounded above" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489910} {:answer/id #uuid "f753fab6-87eb-5f94-97b3-81272950d8ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "bounded below" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490053}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b49aa992-7767-5ec1-abc9-7e510c2fae46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "bounded above" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489910} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfadd8cf-a2e0-5f5b-a357-b9ae83b9b1c7" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490192}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7fdea743-d7bb-5faa-abc9-1bdf19e0dbae" :question/math-academy-id "q-253044" :question/problem "Consider the set $A=(-\\infty ,-1).$ Complete the following reasoning to determine $inf(A)$ and $sup(A).$\n\nThe infimum of $A$ is the {{field-1}} of $A,$ and the supremum is the {{field-2}} of $A.$\n\nSince $A$ is {{field-3}}, we have $inf(A)$ {{field-4}}.\n\nSince $A$ is {{field-5}}, we have $sup(A)$ {{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "The infimum of $A$ is the greatest lower bound of $A,$ and the supremum is the smallest upper bound of $A.$\n\nTo find the infimum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** lower bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of lower bounds) and take the maximum of this set.\n\nSince $A$ is unbounded below, $A$ has no lower bounds, and $inf(A)=-\\infty .$\n\nNext, to find the supremum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- Any number in the set $x\\ge -1$ is greater than or equal to the elements of $A.$ Thus, the set $[-1,\\infty )$ contains only upper bounds of $A.$\n\n- Any number in the set $x<-1$ is **not** an upper bound of $A.$ In other words, we can always find an element of $A$ that is greater than $x$ for any $x<-1.$\n\nTherefore, $[-1,\\infty )$ is the set of upper bounds of $A,$ and\n\n$$\nsup(A)=min[-1,\\infty )=-1.\n$$\n\nThe completed reasoning is given below.\n\nThe infimum of a set $A$ is the $\\text{greatest lower bound}$ of $A,$ and the supremum is the $\\text{smallest upper bound}$ of $A.$\n\nSince $A$ is $\\text{unbounded below},$ we have $inf(A)=-\\infty .$\n\nSince $A$ is $\\text{bounded above},$ we have $sup(A)=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162526 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162158 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe2b2c0-23a0-5bd0-8bc7-c12139820b61" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of a Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16f916cc-94f7-5a71-a178-e1e606a172ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "inf(A)=-1\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489566} {:answer/id #uuid "266c7228-b4bb-5e08-96bf-a8a086712c66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "inf(A)=0\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489601} {:answer/id #uuid "5295bbac-a212-512d-9607-9f1f6bb17448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "inf(A)=-\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489709} {:answer/id #uuid "cfcb399e-74da-5c9e-8dac-e3eed6a5f7de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "inf(A)=-1\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489976} {:answer/id #uuid "d5186c5a-5a30-5325-9bea-58622f595315" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "inf(A)=0\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5295bbac-a212-512d-9607-9f1f6bb17448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "inf(A)=-\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489709} :answer-field/id #uuid "598cb6fa-a32f-51ee-a272-ef449a513971" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160486}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "293c6e17-bbd1-5e99-90f1-bfcaef49f68c" :question/math-academy-id "q-253138" :question/problem "Consider the following set.\n\n$$\nA=\\{n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )\\,:\\,n\\in N\\}\n$$\n\nFor this set, we have that {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The infimum of $A$ is the greatest lower bound of $A.$\n\nTo find the infimum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** lower bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of lower bounds) and take the maximum of this set.\n\nThe elements of $A$ are the terms of the sequence ${a}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi ),\\,n\\in N=\\{1,2,3,4,…\\}.\n$$\n\nLet's draw some points of our sequence on the real line:\n\n![](images/bc/bcece2e5bdef3c9d939d953fbeb0c5163d9343004cd309f28db37bf9b5b089ef.png)\n\nWe see that ${a}_{n}$ is an oscillating, non-convergent sequence. Moreover, $A$ is unbounded below. In other words, we can always find a sufficiently large $n$ so that ${a}_{n}$ is smaller than $x$ for any real number $x.$ Therefore, $A$ has no lower bounds and $inf(A)\\,=-\\infty .$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488227 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162159 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4649783b-3436-55a5-b779-1ca3de17c535" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2439eeb1-f067-5723-ba6c-598c5d8955f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=+\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487640} {:answer/id #uuid "8d3302b8-4e4c-524a-9fcb-03282d5609f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487835} {:answer/id #uuid "b1af54c6-96ae-5f04-9cc5-657032bf0dd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487903} {:answer/id #uuid "f5c1f462-2a1b-56df-a334-da05637bfe75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2439eeb1-f067-5723-ba6c-598c5d8955f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=+\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487640} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5dd2e68-c307-5896-9e28-9a0db4658a38" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488153}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "75529c50-5084-5200-a1d5-34d0fbf018a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-253141" :question/problem "![](images/81/8152677cc952ca219aa9395f3d1a9acbc9379b1cffd0b0f0e6bd0f3f0148632a.png)\n\nWhat is the supremum of the function $y=f(x)$ shown above?\n\n$\\,{sup}_{x\\in R}f(x)$\n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a function is the supremum of the range of the function.\n\nIn this case, the range of $f$ is $A=(-1,\\infty ).$\n\nTo find the supremum of a set $A,$ we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nIn our case, $A$ has no upper bounds. We can always find an element $x$ such that $f(x)$ is greater than $y$ for any $y.$ \n\nTherefore, ${sup}_{x\\in R}f(x)$ $=+\\infty .$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490221 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162158 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe2b2c0-23a0-5bd0-8bc7-c12139820b61" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of a Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10e66bfe-083b-5be0-9583-02c2dd9dbc3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "sup(A)=\\frac{13}{3}\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489555} {:answer/id #uuid "89293f7d-7259-5ca0-9d47-f57a27be0b52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "sup(A)=5\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489831} {:answer/id #uuid "c65bb871-f69d-5809-a2e7-c05b75873a6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$sup(A)$ does not exist" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489944} {:answer/id #uuid "d622005e-b5a8-5b3b-b564-16897d776f36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "sup(A)=5\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489989} {:answer/id #uuid "df7f2a2d-61f7-56a7-bec1-7262e75f747b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "sup(A)=\\frac{13}{3}\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d622005e-b5a8-5b3b-b564-16897d776f36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "sup(A)=5\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489989} :answer-field/id #uuid "236e608b-8ac0-548b-a7ea-fa7e8de10892" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490090}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2472238f-de89-5651-9808-c29025aa1081" :question/math-academy-id "q-253514" :question/problem "Consider the following set.\n\n$$\nA=\\{5-{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n}\\,:\\,n\\in N\\}\n$$\n\nFor this set, we have {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a set $A$ is the smallest upper bound of $A.$\n\nTo find the supremum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nThe elements of $A$ are all the terms of the sequence ${a}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=5-{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n},\\,n\\in N=\\{1,2,3,4,…\\}.\n$$\n\nLet's draw some points of our sequence on the real line:\n\n![](images/1e/1ea2ed214496ed38ae605e9ac64bebd781a0d5529561fce44d98cca6839d6fbb.png)\n\nWe see that ${a}_{n}$ is increasing and converges to $5.$ \n\nSo, in our case, we have that\n\n- any number in the set $x\\ge 5$ is an upper bound of $A,$\n\n- any number in the set $x<5$ is **not** an upper bound of $A.$ In other words, we can always find a sufficiently large $n$ so that $5-{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n}$ is greater than $x$ for any $x<5.$\n\nTherefore, $[5,\\infty )$ is the set of upper bounds of $A,$ and \n\n$$\nsup(A)=min[5,\\infty )=5.\n$$\n\nNotice that $5$ is *not* the maximum of $A$ (the set $A$ has no maximum). Therefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nsup(A)=5\\notin A.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490216 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162156 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f950f3da-81c2-574a-b7f7-06d88945c249" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of a Finite Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3db2d41-9f95-5454-99e3-3731cf3c7216" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3db2d41-9f95-5454-99e3-3731cf3c7216" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489907} :answer-field/id #uuid "641a7bf6-8d64-5bbd-b720-80aba2e3fd36" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490133}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0ecf28e6-85ea-58f8-8358-bdfe911fb50e" :question/math-academy-id "q-253542" :question/problem "What is the infimum of the set $C=\\{-1,\\,-3,\\,0,\\,2,\\,1,\\,-2\\}?$\n\n$inf(C)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The infimum of a set $C$ is the greatest lower bound of $C.$\n\nIf $C$ is a finite set, the infimum of $C$ equals its minimum. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}inf(C) & =min\\{-1,\\,-3,\\,0,\\,2,\\,1,\\,-2\\}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490234 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162156 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f950f3da-81c2-574a-b7f7-06d88945c249" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of a Finite Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dcae1ab-8b52-5672-bb43-dd85e7593b29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3dcae1ab-8b52-5672-bb43-dd85e7593b29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489655} :answer-field/id #uuid "383aa34f-a1d1-5f56-a588-24ec2c1c5712" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "332a6eec-904f-5523-bf1a-c62328e3b046" :question/math-academy-id "q-253552" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined as\n\n$$\nA=\\{(-1)^{n+1}\\cdot n:n\\in \\{1,2,3,4\\}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the supremum of $A?$\n\n$sup(A)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a set $A$ is the smallest upper bound of $A.$\n\nIf $A$ is a finite set, the supremum of $A$ equals its maximum. \n\nFirst, let's write down all the terms of our set by substituting $n=1,2,3,4$ into the expression for the elements of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)^{1+1}\\cdot 1 & =1 \\\\ (-1)^{2+1}\\cdot 2 & =-2 \\\\ (-1)^{3+1}\\cdot 3 & =3 \\\\ (-1)^{4+1}\\cdot 4 & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nA=\\{1,\\,-2,\\,3,\\,-4\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sup(A) & =max\\{1,\\,-2,\\,3,\\,-4\\}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490259 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162157 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fee0e08c-5a7a-5f78-83aa-39679bb3b17b" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of an Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03e1ddde-094e-575d-9216-44ec5195d360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489524} {:answer/id #uuid "3f4f994b-ba11-5ca0-aef7-b28106a79f3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489658} {:answer/id #uuid "4cd1b0f7-d80a-50b7-845c-cc2784569fb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489694} {:answer/id #uuid "f3ccc00a-63f1-5bd8-a453-0e81d703f3e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3ccc00a-63f1-5bd8-a453-0e81d703f3e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490040} :answer-field/id #uuid "149b46b7-83ac-5b5a-b14c-9564fbc3ed3d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490085} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2653f489-1ea3-5e38-8c0d-93a677463b87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/