ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "sup(A)=\\sqrt{5}\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05f23a5e-38cb-539f-b7c3-cad96ff77d21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "sup(A)=\\sqrt{5}\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489526} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e941132-5627-5132-94a5-af608b2e9c1e" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490121} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60fe427a-ec1e-5dc4-943a-75b9d2f36f13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489743} {:answer/id #uuid "635f21bd-99a2-5757-b577-5b099f629363" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489747}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "635f21bd-99a2-5757-b577-5b099f629363" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489747} :answer-field/id #uuid "b76bb8b2-2c1f-5117-8531-fe1007b02a61" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490171}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "64fea66a-24ac-5ed4-9315-868a66adf40d" :question/math-academy-id "q-253555" :question/problem "Consider the set $A=[1,\\sqrt{5}].$ Complete the following reasoning to identify $sup(A).$\n\nThe supremum of a set $A$ is the {{field-1}} of $A.$\n\nThe set of upper bounds of $A$ is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{x\\in R\\,:\\,x{{field-2}}{{field-3}}\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a set $A$ is the smallest upper bound of $A.$\n\nTo find the supremum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- Any number in the set $x\\ge \\sqrt{5}$ is greater than or equal to the elements of $A.$ Thus, the set $[\\sqrt{5},\\infty )$ contains only upper bounds of $A.$\n\n- Any number in the set $x<\\sqrt{5}$ is **not** an upper bound of $A.$ In other words, we can always find an element of $A$ that is greater than $x$ for any $x<\\sqrt{5}.$\n\nTherefore, $[\\sqrt{5},\\infty )$ is the set of upper bounds of $A,$ and\n\n$$\nsup(A)=min\\,[\\sqrt{5},\\infty )=\\sqrt{5}.\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\sqrt{5}$ is also the maximum of $A.$\n\nThe completed reasoning is given below.\n\nThe supremum of $A$ is the $\\text{smallest upper bound}$ of $A.$\n\nThe set of upper bounds of $A$ is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{x\\in R\\,:\\,x\\ge \\sqrt{5}\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $sup(A)=\\sqrt{5}\\in A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488271 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162159 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4649783b-3436-55a5-b779-1ca3de17c535" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67197de5-74fe-5dc0-abe6-0952b996a82d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67197de5-74fe-5dc0-abe6-0952b996a82d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487773} :answer-field/id #uuid "42f7eabb-2484-504e-a47e-b134986a6e92" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ddf4ec2c-4f4d-56c1-bc14-78cfd2f52940" :question/math-academy-id "q-253895" :question/problem "![](images/50/50b52da574101dfca7c620411a446f2c5f3ef41242186ca38da072e140019024.png)\n\nWhat is the supremum of the function $y=f(x)$ shown above?\n\n${sup}_{x\\in R}f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a function is the supremum of the range of the function.\n\nIn this case, the range of $f$ is $A=(-2,3].$\n\nTo find the supremum of a set $A,$ we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nSo, in our case, we have that\n\n- any number $y\\ge 3$ is an upper bound of $A,$\n\n- any number $y<3$ cannot be an upper bound of $A$ because $3,$ an element of $A,$ is greater than $y.$\n\nTherefore, $[3,\\infty )$ is the set of upper bounds of $A,$ and\n\n$$\n{sup}_{x\\in R}f(x)=sup(A)=min[3,\\infty )=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487298 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162159 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4649783b-3436-55a5-b779-1ca3de17c535" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e00bd87d-5f08-5393-9463-9cdcd001373e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e00bd87d-5f08-5393-9463-9cdcd001373e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487081} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c08a640-f274-5c79-a1a1-0eb159327882" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487173}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1a350bae-823f-50ee-90ca-2add36d5d3d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-253896" :question/problem "![](images/0d/0d745d274250c84f6701ff22d17d0c6506a9f03f4a1a461e09f609a0ea11d99b.png)\n\nWhat is the supremum of the function $y=f(x)$ shown above?\n\n${sup}_{x\\in R}f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a function is the supremum of the range of the function.\n\nIn this case, the range of $f$ is $A=[-2,1).$\n\nTo find the supremum of a set $A,$ we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nSo, in our case, we have that\n\n- any number $y\\ge 1$ is an upper bound of $A,$\n\n- any number $y<1$ is **not** an upper bound of $A.$ In other words, we can always find an element of $A$ that is greater than $y$ for any $y<1.$\n\nTherefore, $[1,\\infty )$ is the set of lower bounds of $A,$ and\n\n$$\n{sup}_{x\\in R}f(x)=sup(A)=min[1,\\infty )=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489208 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162159 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4649783b-3436-55a5-b779-1ca3de17c535" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d76112fe-0fce-56ee-bf7a-c6fba9800dcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488914}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d76112fe-0fce-56ee-bf7a-c6fba9800dcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488914} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ed2c775-df54-54e2-ad43-b85dd389a975" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "42308119-ffcd-55c6-b052-68e017e7cc90" :question/math-academy-id "q-253897" :question/problem "![](images/64/64131e649a82e06d2750d53bdf05b1701b0674a05b70149081ddb58d700adb54.png)\n\nWhat is the supremum of the function $y=f(x)$ shown above?\n\n${sup}_{x\\in R}f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a function is the supremum of the range of the function.\n\nIn this case, the range of $f$ is $A=(-1,2).$\n\nTo find the supremum of a set $A,$ we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nSo, in our case, we have that\n\n- any number $y\\ge 2$ is an upper bound of $A,$\n\n- any number $y<2$ is **not** an upper bound of $A.$ In other words, we can always find an element of $A$ that is greater than $y$ for any $y<2.$\n\nTherefore, $[2,\\infty )$ is the set of lower bounds of $A,$ and\n\n$$\n{sup}_{x\\in R}f(x)=sup(A)=min[2,\\infty )=2.\n$$"}]}
